data fold_cons_handler_binder_unbound_on_the_native_resolver: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "fold_cons_handler_binder_unbound_on_the_native_resolver" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**the native resolver does not bind a fold handler's binder -- a `cons: fn(acc, candidate)` handler over fold_list refuses its module at prepare with resolve_reason_unbound_symbol anchored at the fold spine, so a claim that observes a std fn's result by folding over it cannot run on the native route** (INVALID STATE: the same spelling binds on the interpreted floor, so the two routes disagree about an ordinary fold).",
    "RECEIPT (2026-10-02, eager-cat-664, head 17fccbf3f62): `gunbc test '//v2/test/claim/variant_field_native_specimen:all'` (same emitted closure ae6fb52183d56945c0dedad90047279110c416c3f7ea5dcb6b5a10724ab7cff6, built clean, discriminating red and malformed control established): target/v2-native-lane/driver-rows.jsonl records all three identities of v2.test.claim.variant_field_native_specimen (vfb_specimen_binder_present_value_node_binds, vfb_specimen_variant_binder_binds, vfb_specimen_unbound_name_yields_no_candidates) as NativeTestRefused at NativeTestStagePrepare with head reason resolve_reason_unbound_symbol, anchor a fold_list_node spine over the atoms `candidate` and `path` -- the handler binder and the field read through it (candidate.path) in the claim's own cons handler. The same three claims are GREEN on the interpreted floor (gunbc run --claim-run, pool 7223 modules, exit 0).",
    "HARM: any test claim that observes a result by folding over it -- the spelling the floor prefers for list observation -- refuses natively before its subject is reached, so native observations are pushed onto spellings the floor does not prefer, and the two routes' agreement surface shrinks by whole claim modules.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. Not native_infer_accepts_only_bool_and_int_match_scrutinees (stage resolve, not infer; the anchor is a fold spine, not a match). Not a_wildcard_match_arm_resolves_as_an_unbound_name (that class is a wildcard in a match arm; here it is a lambda parameter of a fold handler). Not unapplied_function_value_admitted_at_a_value_position (nothing is admitted; a binder is missing). The closure's pre-existing file refusals in the same run (dag/std/occurrence_identity.dag normalized_tree_reason_wrapper_retention_not_normalized, src/v2/compiler/body_lowering_fold.dag and dag/std/machine_constraints.dag parse_g0_tokens_remain, dag/extdeps/uri_path.dag body_lowering_reason_function_value_body_unread -- 4 file_refusal rows in the terminal tally) are NOT this class: the anchor is in the claim's own handler, and the unbound name is the handler's own binder, not a name from a refused file.",
    "REPAIR RECEIPT (2026-10-08, fierce-fox-380): the native ingest resolver binds a fold handler's parameters as an ordinary Arrow. Evaluated v2.test.claim.resolve.fold_handler_binder_resolve (bounded --entry; the SUBJECT is three ingest strings, not the corpus): fold=resolved, lambda=resolved, undeclared=refused resolve_reason_unbound_symbol at fhb_undeclared_item (sole chain). The fold specimen is `fold(xs, false, fn(acc, candidate) { acc || candidate.path })` -- the same dotted handler spelling the 2026-10-02 native-lane receipt anchored at a fold_list_node spine. Route: native_test_context_from_ingest then native_census_module_resolution. The historical RED is the 2026-10-02 vfb_specimen NativeTestRefused receipt above; this change enrolls the discriminating green and the undeclared-name red. #13028 (lambda-binder projection as lexical reference) is the resolve reading that makes `candidate.path` a BoundInFrame projection once the step Arrow is the Loop positional (fold_recurrence_encoding).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mechanically preventable -- v2.test.claim.resolve.fold_handler_binder_resolve `a_fold_handler_item_binder_resolves`, `a_non_fold_lambda_argument_still_resolves`, `an_undeclared_name_in_a_fold_handler_is_the_sole_refusal_at_its_atom` (native ingest of supplied modules); v2.test.claim.binder_admission.callable_binder_slice `cbs_the_fold_encoding_step_admits_handler_binders_holds` (supplied encoding shape). Invalid unbound handler use is still writable source; the enrolled claims refuse a regression.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. A fold handler's parameter is a lambda over the folded item; binding it is the same Arrow-domain LexicalFrame resolve_arrow_node already opens for any nested function value.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the capability: construction that makes an unbound fold-handler parameter unwritable -- the step Arrow's domain binders are the only names the handler body may take as BoundInFrame, with no second harvest. The three vfb_specimen_* identities passing native prepare remain inhabitance of the same capability on a production claim module and do not raise the rung by themselves.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.resolve.fold_handler_binder_resolve", decl_name: "a_fold_handler_item_binder_resolves", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.resolve.fold_handler_binder_resolve", decl_name: "a_non_fold_lambda_argument_still_resolves", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.resolve.fold_handler_binder_resolve", decl_name: "an_undeclared_name_in_a_fold_handler_is_the_sole_refusal_at_its_atom", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.binder_admission.callable_binder_slice", decl_name: "cbs_the_fold_encoding_step_admits_handler_binders_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
